  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Plastic Waste Management: Towards a New Social Contract in Partnership with the Private sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">The Republic of Djibouti faces major challenges in the collection, management, and treatment of waste&#x2014;especially plastic waste&#x2014;in both urban and rural areas. Municipalities are currently responsible for waste management, but they face significant obstacles: approximately 344 tons of waste are generated daily, of which 20% is plastic&#x2014;a volume that continues to rise due to population growth and urbanization. This situation is further hampered by the lack of official, reliable, and accessible data,</narrative>
  </description>
